WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.261
Subject–Verb Agreement

00:00:02.641 --> 00:00:06.259
Find the real subject. Ignore the words in between.

00:00:07.459 --> 00:00:08.550
How to spot it

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.846
One verb in different forms

00:00:11.396 --> 00:00:14.108
Lots of words between subject and verb

00:00:14.658 --> 00:00:18.673
It’s testing: whether the verb matches its true subject

00:00:19.873 --> 00:00:20.639
The method

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:23.551
Step 1: Find the verb blank

00:00:23.831 --> 00:00:26.445
Ask: who or what is doing this?

00:00:26.995 --> 00:00:29.485
Step 2: Cross out the extras

00:00:29.765 --> 00:00:32.604
“Of the…” phrases and anything between commas.

00:00:33.154 --> 00:00:35.904
Step 3: One or more than one?

00:00:36.184 --> 00:00:38.272
Look at the subject that’s left.

00:00:38.822 --> 00:00:41.128
Step 4: Match the verb

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:45.481
Singular verbs usually end in -s: is, has, shows.

00:00:46.031 --> 00:00:47.126
In a few words

00:00:47.276 --> 00:00:50.631
Cross out. Find the subject. Match.

00:00:51.831 --> 00:00:52.613
The rules

00:00:53.013 --> 00:00:54.768
“Of” phrases don’t count

00:00:55.048 --> 00:00:57.948
Wrong: The box of photos were stored.

00:00:58.228 --> 00:01:00.909
Right: The box of photos was stored.

00:01:01.459 --> 00:01:02.943
A and B = plural

00:01:03.223 --> 00:01:05.911
Wrong: Heat and drought is forcing change.

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:08.906
Right: Heat and drought are forcing change.

00:01:09.456 --> 00:01:11.792
Each, every, the number of = singular

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:15.202
Wrong: Each of the paintings show a stage.

00:01:15.482 --> 00:01:18.543
Right: Each of the paintings shows a stage.

00:01:19.093 --> 00:01:20.396
Groups are singular

00:01:20.676 --> 00:01:23.071
Wrong: The council have voted.

00:01:23.351 --> 00:01:25.549
Right: The council has voted.

00:01:26.099 --> 00:01:28.312
Neither / nor: match the closer noun

00:01:28.592 --> 00:01:32.498
Right: Neither the director nor the actors were willing.

00:01:33.048 --> 00:01:34.976
Flip inverted sentences

00:01:35.256 --> 00:01:38.763
Right: Beneath the temple was a series of tunnels.

00:01:39.963 --> 00:01:41.024
Let’s try one

00:01:41.424 --> 00:01:46.537
The collection of letters written by soldiers during the Civil War ______ historians a rare view

00:01:46.537 --> 00:01:48.819
of daily life in military camps.

00:01:49.469 --> 00:01:54.255
Cross out the of phrase: of letters written by soldiers during the Civil War.

00:01:54.805 --> 00:02:00.308
What’s left? The collection. That’s one thing, so the verb must be singular.

00:02:00.858 --> 00:02:06.854
Offer, have offered, and are offering are all plural. Offers is singular. Choice C.

00:02:08.054 --> 00:02:09.123
Common traps

00:02:09.523 --> 00:02:10.662
The nearest noun

00:02:10.942 --> 00:02:14.034
The noun right before the verb is usually a decoy.

00:02:14.584 --> 00:02:15.899
Flipped sentences

00:02:16.179 --> 00:02:18.873
Sometimes the subject comes after the verb.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.733
Subject–Verb Agreement

00:02:22.013 --> 00:02:25.369
Cross out. Find the subject. Match.

00:02:25.919 --> 00:02:26.499
Spot it

00:02:26.699 --> 00:02:29.699
One verb in different forms (is / are, has / have)

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:30.956
Steps

00:02:31.156 --> 00:02:34.035
1. Find the verb: who or what is doing it?

00:02:34.315 --> 00:02:37.407
2. Cross out “of…” phrases + comma extras

00:02:37.687 --> 00:02:39.625
3. One thing or more than one?

00:02:39.905 --> 00:02:43.290
4. Match the verb (singular often ends in -s)

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:44.565
Remember

00:02:44.765 --> 00:02:47.317
“of” phrases never change the subject

00:02:47.597 --> 00:02:49.080
A and B → plural

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.685
each, every, the number of → singular

00:02:51.965 --> 00:02:54.164
team, council, group → singular

00:02:54.444 --> 00:02:57.129
neither / nor → match the closer noun

00:02:57.679 --> 00:02:58.120
Trap

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.147
The noun right before the verb

00:03:00.897 --> 00:03:04.315
Pause the video now, and copy this page into your notes.
